<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<chapter xml:id="ch14-greens-theorem" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Green's Theorem and the Beginning of Stokes' Idea</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>Green's theorem connects the line integrals of Chapter 13 with the double integrals of Chapter 10. Circulation around a boundary measures the accumulated scalar curl inside; outward flux measures accumulated divergence. We track the orientation of every boundary component and use a locally defined exterior derivative to express both statements in the same notation.</p>
  </introduction>

